[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) closed with one line: "all 412 are one issue." Read the export
the way `fingerprint.ts` reads it — by the reporter's place and the server code, not the
subject intake guessed — and the night held **three issues**, not one.

<ClusterTable ticket={4471} />

## What was really in the queue

- **`sched-prod:E-TZ-114`** — the ticket's own issue. Thursday's shifts shown an hour late.
  Fixed by change #29 at 06:15; the queue went quiet.
- **`tram-3:E-TZ-114`** — same code, different place: a different bug by the desk's own rule.
  Departure boards and platform screens an hour behind the timetable; "next tram in 61
  minutes, it is here now". Merged into #4471 anyway. No ticket of its own.
- **`rota-6:E-SYNC-04`** — not a timezone bug at all. The night rota listed twice, an hour
  apart, "which one is real?" Six of these reports were mis-tagged `sched-prod` by intake.
  No ticket of its own.

<Callout kind="warn">
Client codes ride along in report bodies — E-UI-31 screens reloading, E-NET-03 offline.
Worth reading, never what a report is filed under. They are not tickets.
</Callout>

## What the count hides

- The export carries **427 rows for 412 reports**: the ticket system exports in overlapping
  pages, and fifteen reports are in it twice. `uniqueById` collapses them — 412 is real, but
  only after dedupe.
- **R-41200 is not a report.** It is the 03:12 job's own output — "status: clean
  (E-TZ-114)" — merged at 05:00 with everything else. The job saw the error code at 03:12
  and called the run clean; the first human report landed at 03:19.
- Merging ran **05:00 → 06:27** while reports still arrived. For twenty-two minutes after
  the fix, new reports kept landing in a ticket already closed — including rota-6 and tram-3
  reports nobody ever opened.

<QueueTimeline ticket={4471} />

## Lessons

- Subject matching merged fast and merged wrong. Two of the three issues in this ticket had
  no ticket of their own when the desk declared "one issue, one fix".
- Merge on place and server code (`fingerprint`), not on the subject a tired reporter typed
  at 4 a.m. — see [decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) for the rule that
  caused this.
- The export is the ground truth; a page is a claim. The table and the chart above are
  computed from the data at render — if the export changes, this page shows it.

<RenderStamp {signature} />
